  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA deepening low pressure system will approach the Ohio Valley from \nthe west later today. Ahead of the low, cloud cover increases and \nsoutherly flow lifts temperatures into the 60s by the afternoon. A \nmodest increase in moisture will be felt with dew points getting \ninto the 40s. \n\nThe slowly strengthening low moves through the Ohio Valley tonight \nalong with a cold front. Showers, and possibly some thunder, are \nexpected in the warm sector east of the low. Instability appears to \nbe very limited by the time the forcing arrives, likely keeping the \nlow end threat for severe storms to the west. Progressive storm \nmotion limits forecast storm total QPF to 0.5\" or less for most \nlocations. \n\nWinds shift to the northwest behind the low Thursday morning \nadvecting in much colder air through Monday. Winds gusts upwards of \n25 mph are possible in the wake of the low on Thursday as the low \ncontinues deepening and the pressure gradient tightens behind the \nlow. Gusty northwesterly flow persists until Sunday although winds \nshould slowly slacken a little each day. Forecast highs remain in the\n40s through Monday with the northwesterly flow behind the low. Some \nperiods of showers are in the forecast for Thursday and Friday as \nshortwave upper level troughs pivot through the Ohio Valley. A few \nwet snowflakes could mix into the rain showers on Friday. \nPrecipitation chances end by the weekend.",
